{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017bywntrDm5AQ14xZnP8Qag","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2024 instruction for reviews reviewer form rating scale site:2024.corl.org\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instructions for Presentations\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instructions-for-presentations\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Call for Workshops\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/call-for-workshops\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Papers XX\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/program/papers-xx\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Demos\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/program/demos\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Papers\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/program/papers\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Speakers\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/program/speakers\"}]\n\nI found the CoRL 2024 Instruction for Reviews page. Based on the search results, the page contains guidance about the review process, reviewer qualifications, and evaluation criteria. However, the specific content about the reviewer form rating scale doesn't appear to be fully captured in the search results shown.\n\nFrom what's visible in the search results, I can tell you that:\n\nResults will be judged on the degree to which they have been objectively established and/or their potential for scientific and technological impact, as well as their relevance to robotic learning. Additionally, reviewers need to have expertise in robotics, robot learning, machine learning and complementary fields, and ideally have a minimum of 3 first author publications in major robotics conferences and journals.\n\nThe full details about the specific rating scale used in the reviewer form would be on the actual Instruction for Reviews page at https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews. You may need to visit that page directly to see the complete rating scale information if it's not fully displayed in the search results.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1f5e0932-32f2-4b4b-9817-0d2ade2fda2a","uuid":"4a57ba0e-21a9-4e12-881f-ebf6a16681e8","timestamp":"2026-05-15T16:27:08.521Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2024 instruction for reviews reviewer form rating scale site:2024.corl.org","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01RkMJnpXEu91LuCyDoXYFTp","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2024","url":"https://2024.corl.org/"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instructions for Presentations","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instructions-for-presentations"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Call for Workshops","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/call-for-workshops"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Call for Papers","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Papers XX","url":"https://2024.corl.org/program/papers-xx"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Demos","url":"https://2024.corl.org/program/demos"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Papers","url":"https://2024.corl.org/program/papers"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Speakers","url":"https://2024.corl.org/program/speakers"}]},"I found the CoRL 2024 Instruction for Reviews page. Based on the search results, the page contains guidance about the review process, reviewer qualifications, and evaluation criteria. However, the specific content about the reviewer form rating scale doesn't appear to be fully captured in the search results shown.\n\nFrom what's visible in the search results, I can tell you that:\n\nResults will be judged on the degree to which they have been objectively established and/or their potential for scientific and technological impact, as well as their relevance to robotic learning. Additionally, reviewers need to have expertise in robotics, robot learning, machine learning and complementary fields, and ideally have a minimum of 3 first author publications in major robotics conferences and journals.\n\nThe full details about the specific rating scale used in the reviewer form would be on the actual Instruction for Reviews page at https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews. You may need to visit that page directly to see the complete rating scale information if it's not fully displayed in the search results."],"durationSeconds":5.214069389999997}}
