{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019AvZzJwr24e6nUzEn9CtcD","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL OpenReview review form \"overall recommendation\" \"strong accept\" \"weak accept\" \"borderline\" \"weak reject\" \"strong reject\"\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Default Review Form | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://docs.openreview.net/reference/default-forms/default-review-form\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CVPR 2026 Reviewer Training Material\",\"url\":\"https://cvpr.thecvf.com/Conferences/2026/ReviewerTrainingMaterial\"},{\"title\":\"ICML 2024 Reviewer Instructions\",\"url\":\"https://icml.cc/Conferences/2024/ReviewerInstructions\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2022 Reviewer Instructions\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"Uncertainty in Artificial Intelligence\",\"url\":\"https://www.auai.org/uai2023/reviewing_instructions\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"Under review as a conference paper at ICLR 2024\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/pdf/e55f3cb39892682f5c37efa8b008171b91981671.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"OpenReviewer: A Specialized Large Language Model for Generating Critical Scientific Paper Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2412.11948v3\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about OpenReview review forms and recommendation scales, though the specific results don't show a CoRL-specific form with exactly those recommendation options (\"strong accept,\" \"weak accept,\" \"borderline,\" \"weak reject,\" \"strong reject\").\n\nHere's what I found:\n\n## OpenReview Default Form\n\nThe OpenReview default review form uses a numeric rating scale with options including \"9: Top 15% of accepted papers, strong accept\", \"8: Top 50% of accepted papers, clear accept\", \"7: Good paper, accept\", \"6: Marginally above acceptance threshold\", \"5: Marginally below acceptance threshold\", \"4: Ok but not good enough - rejection\", \"3: Clear rejection\", \"2: Strong rejection\", and \"1: Trivial or wrong\".\n\n## CoRL Review Guidelines\n\nCoRL's review form asks for an evaluation of the originality, quality, clarity, significance, relevance and limitations of the work, but the search results don't show the specific \"overall recommendation\" field options you mentioned for CoRL.\n\nThe search results show that different conferences use varying recommendation scales. Some use terminology like \"borderline accept\" and \"borderline reject,\" while others use numeric scales. If you're looking for the specific CoRL OpenReview form with those exact recommendation options, you may need to check the CoRL 2026 call for papers or reviewer instructions directly on their official website.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1f5e0932-32f2-4b4b-9817-0d2ade2fda2a","uuid":"f1726481-dc1b-4086-bd9f-48f0bac49739","timestamp":"2026-05-15T16:27:43.546Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL OpenReview review form \"overall recommendation\" \"strong accept\" \"weak accept\" \"borderline\" \"weak reject\" \"strong reject\"","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01JdWYJY3FbWfqhg2PLH5bzL","content":[{"title":"Default Review Form | OpenReview","url":"https://docs.openreview.net/reference/default-forms/default-review-form"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CVPR 2026 Reviewer Training Material","url":"https://cvpr.thecvf.com/Conferences/2026/ReviewerTrainingMaterial"},{"title":"ICML 2024 Reviewer Instructions","url":"https://icml.cc/Conferences/2024/ReviewerIns