luation\nM6 (Desirable): Per-seed variance for per-perturbation tables\n\n### Key Minor Issues\n- Incomplete bibliography (MoIRA, CORAL, LoRA-SP mentioned without citations)\n- E2E training objective unspecified (how does gradient flow through soft routing?)\n- Cross-type degradation claim misleading (-20% is not vs frozen but vs own-type)\n- Unclear evaluation episode count\n\n---\n\n## R2 Review (Novelty + Related Work)\n\n### Strengths\nS1: Core insight well-motivated (SAFE detects but doesn't correct; Meta-Brain does both)\nS2: Thorough experimental design within scope (ablation ladder decomposition is informative)\nS3: Cross-backbone validation strengthens generality claim\nS4: Well-structured narrative\n\n### Weaknesses\nW1 (Major): Limited novelty — straightforward composition of known components (linear probe + MoE routing + LoRA). \"New routing dimension\" (perturbation type) is an application insight, not methodological advance.\nW2 (Major): Severely incomplete related work. Only 8 references total. Missing: LoRAMoE, MoLoRA, MixLoRA, MOELoRA, LoRA-Switch, AdapterFusion, Poly, TENT/TTT, PaliGemma, Alain & Bengio probing, MoE fundamentals (Shazeer). MoIRA/CORAL/LoRA-SP mentioned by name without citations.\nW3 (Major): Cross-backbone VLA-GSE comparison confounded (same as R1-W3).\nW4 (Major): Three \"contributions\" are really one contribution repackaged (observation + system + consequence).\nW5 (Moderate): Routing setting too easy (F1=0.993). Missing rank-48 universal baseline to test if sufficient capacity eliminates need for routing.\nW6 (Moderate): Sim-only. 3-class taxonomy designed for LIBERO-Plus's controlled perturbation set.\nW7 (Minor): CM adds complexity for modest gain (same as R1-W7).\n\n### Missing References\n- MoIRA, CORAL, LoRA-SP (mentioned without citations)\n- LoRAMoE, MoLoRA, MixLoRA, MOELoRA, LoRA-Switch\n- AdapterFusion, Poly, AdaMix\n- TENT, TTT\n- PaliGemma [Beyer et al. 2024]\n- Linear probing foundations [Alain & Bengio 2017]\n- MoE fundamentals [Shazeer et al. 2017]\n- Original LIBERO benchmark\n\n### Key Minor Issues\n- No architecture figure\n- No t-SNE visualization of perturbation clusters\n- Concurrent submission citations (LIBERO-Plus CVPR 2026, VLA-GSE CoRL 2026)\n- All results suspiciously even integers\n- Overall average discrepancy (53.67 rounds to 53.7, not 53.6)\n\n---\n\n## Your Task\n\nPerform Steps 2 and 3 of the roundtable:\n\n**Step 2 (Cross-sharing):** For each reviewer, identify:\n- Points from the other reviewer that they would likely agree with\n- Points they would likely push back on\n- New insights that emerge from comparing both reviews\n\n**Step 3 (Convergence):** Synthesize into:\n1. **Agreed strengths** (both reviewers concur)\n2. **Agreed weaknesses** (both reviewers concur)\n3. **Disputed points** (reviewers disagree — state both sides)\n4. **Severity assessment**: For each agreed weakness, assess whether it is addressable in a revision or fundamental\n5. **Preliminary score range**: Based on the convergence, what score range (on 1-10) does each reviewer likely gravitate toward? Provide reasoning.\n\nBe specific and analytical. Don't just list — synthesize and judge."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01CQSAAuknMmVcs6rAKpCSTu","session_id":"1f5e0932-32f2-4b4b-9817-0d2ade2fda2a","uuid":"da44af74-ce2b-43c2-9075-88c4a74d55ca","timestamp":"2026-05-15T16:32:31.267Z"}
